An edit of snowfall-village-raw.png:
Use your image generation tool to EDIT the attached image and produce exactly ONE image: a flat segmentation mask of it. Paint the open night sky (everything that is sky, including the moon, stars and clouds, down to the mountain ridges and treetops) in solid pure blue (#0000FF). Paint every snow-covered surface that snow would settle on (the snow on the roofs, the snowy ground, paths and banks, the snow capping the walls and fence posts, and snow lying on the trees and bushes) in solid pure red (#FF0000). Paint everything else (the mountains, forests, lake, castle, church, house walls, windows, chimneys, fences, tree trunks and dark foliage) in solid pure black. Follow the outlines exactly, at the same positions. No shading, no texture, no other colors. Keep the same 1536x1024 size. Save the generated image into the current directory as snowfall-village-mask.png (copy it from wherever the tool writes it, do not resize or edit it). Print only the saved path. Do nothing else.
